---
import { withBase } from '../../data/site';
import { UI, type Lang } from '../../data/i18n';

const { lang } = Astro.props;
const ui = UI[lang];
const base = lang === 'en' ? '/en' : '';
---

<section class="hero">
  <span class="eyebrow">{ui.homeEyebrow}</span>
  <h1 class="name">蔡骥淳 <span class="hand">Joe Cai</span></h1>
  <p class="now">{ui.homeTagline}</p>
</section>

{
  lang === 'zh' ? (
    <section class="prose-home" style="margin-top:1.8rem">
      <p>
        我关注一个问题：<a href={withBase('/projects/#memloom')}>让模型记住人</a>。
        对话结束之后，模型能不能记得住、想得起、用得上？为此我在做
        <a href={withBase('/projects/#memloom')}>MemLoom</a>
        —— 一套把 LLM 从热路径上挪出去的记忆系统；同时持续对比评测主流方案（HMS、mem0、EgoLife）。
      </p>
      <p>
        我相信克制的设计和扎实的工程是同一件事：把复杂性收进去，把简洁留给使用者。
        偶尔也做点小而美的东西，比如信纸质感的微信小程序原型「<a href={withBase('/projects/')}>回信</a>」。
      </p>
      <p>
        平时写点<a href={withBase('/blog/')}>技术笔记</a>，也翻译喜欢的长文。
        关于职业选择，我译过一篇很喜欢的文章：<a href={withBase('/blog/pick-a-career/')}
          >《如何选择一份真正适合你的职业》</a
        >。
      </p>
    </section>
  ) : (
    <section class="prose-home" style="margin-top:1.8rem">
      <p>
        I keep coming back to one question: <a href={withBase('/en/projects/#memloom')}
          >can models remember people</a
        >? Long after a conversation ends — can a model recall, retrieve, and actually use what it
        learned? That's why I'm building <a href={withBase('/en/projects/#memloom')}>MemLoom</a>,
        a memory system that keeps LLMs off the hot path, while continuously benchmarking
        mainstream approaches (HMS, mem0, EgoLife).
      </p>
      <p>
        I believe restraint in design and solid engineering are the same discipline: tuck the
        complexity away, leave the simplicity for the user. Now and then I build small, quiet
        things — like 「<a href={withBase('/en/projects/')}>回信</a>」, a letter-paper WeChat
        mini-program prototype.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write <a href={withBase('/en/blog/')}>technical notes</a> and translate long-form essays
        I love. On career choices, I translated a favorite:
        <a href={withBase('/blog/pick-a-career/')}><em>How to Pick a Career (That Actually Fits You)</em></a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  )
}

<section class="home-section">
  <h2>{ui.homeDir}</h2>
  <ul class="link-row">
    <li><a href={withBase(`${base}/work`)}>{ui.homeWork}</a></li>
    <li><a href={withBase(`${base}/projects/`)}>{ui.homeProjects}</a></li>
    <li><a href={withBase(`${base}/blog/`)}>{ui.homeBlog}</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <h2>{ui.homeFind}</h2>
  <ul class="link-row">
    <li><a href="https://github.com/jichuncai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
    <li><a href="mailto:joe@example.com">Email</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>
